            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Peter Barnes first started his career in respiratory research in the late 1970s following studies at the Universities of Oxford and Cambridge. He is currently Professor of Thoracic Medicine at the National Heart and Lung Institute, Head of Respiratory Medicine at Imperial College and Honorary Consultant Physician at the Royal Brompton Hospital. He speaks to Future Medicinal Chemistry about the molecular mechanisms currently under investigation by his group, and discusses his views on the latest therapeutic breakthroughs and the future of respiratory research.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
